From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:17:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 55/57] docs, z63-tools: the body MCU's lens side, recovered
 from its own image

docs/mcu-ex/lens.md (Chinese) reads ex2010_0200a0.bi's lens modules and
the EXPEED's side of them. The MCU never talks to the lens: it detects it
(PG0, active low, debounced), switches two power paths (PB0, PA9, make
before break), sets PF12/PD15 and latches PG4, and speaks provider 13 to
the EXPEED (kinds 1..5, replies 0x81..0x85, unsolicited 0x91 attach and
0x96 boot power-up). The EXPEED runs the lens link itself: serial
instance 3 at 8 MHz, pin 58 wake, pin 41 ready, 0x55 frames, and an
83-step connect sequence. docs/mcu-ex/eg/ has the command dictionary and
step tables; docs/mcu-ex-plan.md the plan.

z63-tools/mcu-ex/: names.json and apply_names.py (214 names for the MCU
image), pins.py and m4mem.py (read the MCU's runtime tables through the
gdbstub's second inferior), lensfields.py (which reply byte a lens field
is), egmem.py/steps.py/findq.py, and the run scripts used for the
hot-plug and step traces.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
