+# EXPEED (eg) side of the lens: MCU provider 13, the lens service, the lens link
+
+Source: z63_eg.elf (idasql 8084, read-only), decompile cache claude-work/dc.
+Every address is eg unless marked MCU. "inferred" marks what the code does
+not state outright. Machine-readable dumps beside this file:
+`eg-lenscmd.txt` (lens command dictionary), `eg-steps.txt` (all 155 step
+records), `eg-seq.txt` (the first 83 steps decoded), tools in `egtools/`.
+
+RAM <-> image: the initialised data the RTOS copies to RAM is at image
+VA = RAM - 0x9BD60F000 for the ranges used here (checked on the codec
+objects 0xA0298B5xx and the lens command table 0xA02B4B350, both
+structured). It is NOT valid everywhere: 0xA02AFF000-0xA02B2D000 maps onto
+UTF-16 Italian help text, so 0xA02AFF508 (the lens serial config, below) has
+to be read from a running machine.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Family 13 codec (MCU provider 13)
+
+Provider table 0x441b5f58, 32-byte rows {id, register, recv, codec getter}
+(family 1 = {1, 0x4117edb8, 0x4117ede4, 0x4100cc78}, family 9 =
+{9, 0x4117cf44, 0x4117cf48, 0x41011148}, family 10 = {0xa, 0x41185d94,
+0x41185dc0, 0x41010bd8} -- these match nikon-z63-mcu.h). Family 13 row
+0x441b60d8: register **0x411832d0** (stores the transport send fn/ctx at
+0xA04CED460/468), recv **0x411832fc**, codec getter **0x4100fcb8** ->
+object 0xA0298B5F0 (image 0x4537C5F0) = {encode 0x4100fccc, meta
+0x4100fdc4, decode 0x4100fdf4}. Row table off_441B7010, 24-byte rows
+{encoder, meta, decoder}:
+
+| row | kind | encoder / decoder | notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | 0x01 | enc 0x4100fea4 | 16 B |
+| 2 | 0x02 | enc 0x4100ff24 | 16 B |
+| 3 | 0x03 | enc 0x4100ffa4 | 16 B, three params |
+| 4 | 0x04 | enc 0x41010030 | 16 B |
+| 5 | 0x05 | enc 0x410100b0 | 12 B |
+| 6..10 | 0x81..0x85 | dec 0x41010130, 0x410101a0, 0x41010210, 0x41010280, 0x410102f0 | |
+| 11 | 0x91 | dec 0x41010370 | |
+| 12 | 0x96 | dec 0x410103e8 | |
+
+Encoders: input descriptor {u8 kind, ptr S}; S is the 16-byte request the
+callers build on the stack and pass by value:
+
+```
+S+0  u8  kind            -> wire[0]
+S+1  u8  sequence id     -> wire[4]
+S+4  u32 (0)             -> wire[5]   (low byte)
+S+8  u16 (0)             -> wire[6..7]
+S+10 u16 (0x0100)        -> wire[8..9]   (the constant [9]=1)
+S+12 u32 param           -> wire[12]  (kinds 1, 2, 4)
+kind 3: S+12 -> [12], S+16 -> [13], S+20 -> [14]
+kind 5: 12 bytes; S+8 -> [6..7], S[10] -> [8], S[11] -> [9]
+```
+Output {0xA0406DC70, u32 length 16 (12 for kind 5), u32 queue class 1,
+u32 type = kind}. Queue class 1 = frame route 2 (as on the Z 8, and as
+logged).
+
+Decoders: each copies kind, [4] seq, [5] status (u32), [6..9] into a record
+(0x81: 0xA0406DB88, 0x82: 0xA0406DBA8, 0x85: 0xA0406DC08, 0x91:
+0xA0406DC30, 0x96: 0xA0406DC50) and returns {type, ptr record}. 0x85 adds
+[12] -> rec+12 and [13] -> rec+16; 0x91 and 0x96 add [12] -> rec+12.
+
+Recv 0x411832fc: 0x81..0x85 -> loc_411836f4(index 0..4, rec) = the
+completion callback stored for that kind by sub_411836b8 (slots
+0xA04CED4A8[0..4]); 0x91 -> callback 0xA04CED470(0x03070011, rec); 0x96 ->
+callback(0x03070012, rec).
+
+## 2. Lens-MCU control module 0x41182064..0x41185300 (inferred name "LMC")
+
+Senders (one per kind): 0x411833fc (1), 0x41183474 (2), 0x411834ec (3),
+0x41183558 (4), 0x411835d0 (5); each stores its completion callback and
+calls the transport (0xA04CED460). They have no static callers: they are
+reached through the interface object at 0xA04CED448 (+32 kind 1, +40 kind 2,
++48 kind 3, +56 kind 4, +64 kind 5), built at run time.
+
+Public API (called by the lens service): 0x41182ec0 (kind 1), 0x41182f08
+(kind 2), 0x41182f50 (kind 3, 24-byte arg), 0x41182f9c (kind 4), 0x41182fe4
+(kind 5): copy the request to 0xA02AFF9E8.. / 9F8 / A08 / A20 / A30, save
+the caller's callback (sub_4118364c slot n), set bit 1<<n on event flag
+0xA04CED3C0. Task entry 0x4118272c (created by 0x41182684, mask 0x1fff):
+
+* bits 0x01..0x10: send kind 1..5 through 0xA04CED448, arm timer 0xA04CED418
+  for **100** ticks (sub_40d32150), current kind in 0xA04CED450;
+* bits 0x20..0x200: a reply came (0x81..0x85): stop the timer and call the
+  caller's callback with event **0x03070020 | n** (sub_41183688) and the
+  decoded record;
+* bit 0x400 (0x91, set by sub_41182d48 on 0x03070011): forward
+  **0x03070001** + record (copied to 0xA02AFFA3C) to the callback registered
+  by sub_41182e58 (0xA04CED458);
+* bit 0x800 (0x96, 0x03070012): forward **0x03070010** + record (0xA02AFFA4C).
+
+Wrappers used by the lens service (build S, seq, callback): 0x4109521c
+kind 1 (mode), 0x41095258 kind 2 (level), 0x41087b08 -> 0x41182f50 kind 3,
+0x41095300 kind 4 (S+12 = arg != 0), 0x41095348 kind 5.
+
+The same module also carries the lens LINK request path: 0x4118302c
+(called from 0x41096398 and 0x41087a60) repacks a link request and hands it
+to the lens transport 0x4117afb4 (section 4), callback 0x41182e28.
+
+## 3. The lens service and its connect sequence
+
+Top-level: 0x41062940 (called from 0x41069338 when its arg is 2) registers
+the MCU event callback **0x41062a58** with 0x41182e58, the sequence
+callbacks (sub_4107d014), and a debug shell command "lensdbg" (string at
+RAM 0xA02B4AB22: "lensdbg", "LnsInf", "LnsPsInf"; sub_40c01534).
+
+0x41062a58 on 0x03070001 (MCU 0x91, lens attach report): rec+4 = MCU status
+([5]), rec+12 = attached ([12]); compares with the current lens state
+(sub_41069a7c: 0 none, 1 attached, 2 = a third state, inferred
+"attached-but-other"), records it (sub_41071bcc -> 0xA02995C18) and starts
+the connect (1) or disconnect (0) flow via sub_4107d05c -> sub_41071b14.
+A nonzero status store item 0x294 (sub_40d77928(0x294)) forces "attached"
+(inferred: a debug/demo setting). On 0x03070010 (MCU 0x96) with rec+12 == 1
+it calls sub_4107289c(2) and sets flag 2 on 0xA048313F8.
+
+### Sequence engine
+
+sub_4107d730 runs a step table at RAM **0xA02B44DE0** (image 0x45535de0),
+32-byte records {start fn, done fn, check fn, param}; current step index
+0xA02995F84 (valid 0..0x52; 155 records exist, the ones after 0x52 belong
+to other sequences, inferred). The start fn sends one request; the done fn
+reads the reply and writes the next step index. Failure path sub_4107daa0:
+the check fn fills {retries 0xA04843389, wait 0xA04843388} (for lens commands
+check 0x41096a3c reads the command record's +40/+44, e.g. 0x0a04 = 10
+retries, 4 ticks apart -- unit inferred ms); when retries run out the
+sequence ends with code 3 and step index 3. 80 (0x50) ends a sequence as
+done (the completion 0xA04843440 is called with {0}). Check fns:
+0x41083c04 = MCU kind 2 step, 0x41083bf4 = MCU kind 1, 0x41083c24 = MCU kind
+4, 0x41096a3c = lens command (param = command index), 0x4108a010/0x41083c14
+other.
+
+The ML (Z-mount) connect sequence, steps 0..82 decoded in `eg-seq.txt`.
+The head of it:
+
+| step | request | then |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0 | MCU kind 2 [12]=0 (0x41087b8c) | 1 (or 81) |
+| 1 | MCU kind 1 mode 0 (0x41087c80) | 3 |
+| 2 | MCU kind 4 arm (0x41087d20) | 3 |
+| 3 | MCU kind 1 mode 2 (0x41087dc8; also sub_41095028(6)) | next from done 0x41087e04 |
+| 4 | lens cmd idx 6, code 0x1F, after the wake handshake (0x41084230) | 11 / 5 / 80 |
+| 5 | cmd 0x1F again | 6 / 80 |
+| 6 / 11 | cmd 0x10 (28 B) | 7 / 12 |
+| 7 / 12 | cmd 0x11 (74 B) | 8 |
+| 8 | cmd 0x30 | 80 |
+| 9 | cmd 0x52 | 10 |
+| 10 | cmd 0x31 | 11 |
+| 13 | cmd 0x12 (66 B) | 80 / ... |
+| 14 | MCU kind 2 [12]=1 (0x41088af0) | 15 |
+| 15..20 | cmd 0x13, 0x24, 0x1024, 0x224, 0x1224, 0x15 | ... |
+| 32 | MCU kind 2 [12]=1 (0x4108a23c) | 33 |
+| 33..79 | mostly cmd 0x70 (the extended group) sub-commands, 0x78, 0x75, 0x7E, 0x76, 0x278 | ... |
+| 80 | MCU kind 2 [12]=0 (0x4108ea54) | 81 |
+| 81 | MCU kind 1 mode 0 (0x4108eb40) | 3 |
+
+So, from the EXPEED's side (inferred from order): **mode 2 is "lens powered
+for communication"**, set right before the first exchange; **mode 0 is
+off**; the MCU's kind 2 level (MCU PF12) goes to **1 only after the
+identification commands 0x10/0x11/0x12 succeeded** (step 14) and back to 0
+at power-down (steps 0, 80) -- inferred "second lens supply / full-power
+enable". Kind 1 mode 1 is used only outside steps 0..82 (0x41091224, step
+record 102), and kind 4/5 by 0x4107e8a8 / 0x4107e99c (lens-detect logic).
+
+**The QEMU loop explained:** steps 0 -> 1 -> 3 -> 4; step 4's wake handshake
+gets no answer from a lens (section 4), step 4 fails, and the flow powers
+down and retries -- the observed kind 2 0 / mode 0 / mode 2 repetition.
+
+### Sysc layer
+
+Sysc controller ids (table 0x4408a4b0, {id, name, handler}): 5 Lens ->
+0x40d6b7a0 (object 0x4408d2f8), 6 MlLens -> 0x40d6b91c (object 0x4408d320,
+"ML_LENS"), 7 FLens -> 0x40d6b154 ("F_LENS"). Commands (table 0x4408a5e8,
+0x58-byte rows): 0x2f MlLensConnect, 0x30 MlLensDisconnect, 0x31
+FLensConnect, 0x32 FLensDisconnect, 0x33 LensConnectCheckComplete, 0x34
+MlLensConnectStartupComplete, 0x35 MlLensConnectComplete, 0x36
+MlLensDisconnectComplete, 0x37 MlLensDisconnectShutdownComplete, 0x38..0x3a
+the F-lens completes; 0x2f-0x30, 0x33-0x37 go to controller 6, 0x31-0x32,
+0x38-0x3a to 7. The MlLens controller (state 0xA035CB2B8, handlers
+0x40d6bc7c, 0x40d6c0a8..0x40d6c1c8) takes the lens service's events
+0x04080005..0x04080009 and posts 0x34 / 0x35 / 0x36 (sub_40d66e7c(52/53/54,
+ok)); the FLens one takes 0x04080005/06 and 0x0408000a/b/c and posts
+0x31/0x32/0x38/0x39/0x3a (0x40d6b210, 0x40d6b694). Which service step
+raises which 0x0408000x was not traced (open).
+
+## 4. The lens link (the EXPEED talks to the lens itself)
+
+Transport task **0x4117a310** (flag 0xA04CE3648, created by 0x4117a23c),
+requests via 0x4117afb4 (copies an 0x58-byte request to 0xA04CE3708 and
+wakes the task). Hardware, opened by **0x4117ad38**:
+
+| what | id | resolved (inferred from the pin-id rule) | use |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| serial | resource 2 -> **instance 3** (sub_40c0040c, table 0x44b16448: 346-343) | one of the 12 controllers at 0x0e700000 | the lens data |
+| pin 41 | GPIO **port 3 bit 10** | interrupt input, ISR **0x4117b338** (config 0x44ae63f0) | lens -> body handshake ("ready") |
+| pin 58 | GPIO **port 4 bit 11** | output (sub_4117b148 / 0x4117b210) | body -> lens wake/request |
+| pin 59 | port 4 bit 12 | set to 1 at init (sub_40c15c7c) | inferred line enable |
+| pin 60 | port 4 bit 13 | set to 1 at init | inferred line enable |
+| timers | sub_40c003b8(4), (1) -> 0xA04CE36A0/A4 | hardware timers | inter-frame timing |
+
+Pin rule: the pin-id table (0x44b15e54, set via 0x41187a24 -> 0x40c00350)
+is the identity; the known ids give id + 1 = 16 * (port - 1) + bit (33 =
+port 3 bit 2, 34 = port 3 bit 3, 38 = port 3 bit 7, 43 = port 3 bit 12, 50
+= port 4 bit 3, all from nikon-z63-mcu.h). Resolving 41/58/59/60 with it
+is inferred; confirm on a running machine (handles 0xA02C29000[id], +4
+port, +8 bit).
+
+GPIO API (handle {+4 port, +8 bit, +12.. capability bytes, +32 irq}):
+0x40c15bb8 write data, 0x40c15bfc read data, 0x40c15c38 / 0x40c15c7c /
+0x40c15cc0 three other per-pin registers (tables 0xA02DC4280 / 4348 /
+4410+44D8; inferred pull / direction / function), 0x40c15dfc irq trigger
+config, 0x40c15f80 irq enable(1)/disable(0), 0x40c16148 irq off.
+
+**Wake handshake** (0x4117b210(1), used by every lens transaction when the
+link is idle, 0x41084230 / 0x41083c38): drive pin 58 (sub_40c15cc0(h,1,1),
+sub_40c15c7c(h,1)), then wait up to **200** ticks for flag bit 1 on
+0xA04CE36C8, which the pin-41 ISR 0x4117b338 sets. Release (arg 0):
+sub_40c15c7c(h,0), sub_40c15c38(h,1), sub_40c15cc0(h,0,1), drive 0. If no
+answer: sub_41083e20 (error) -- this is where the QEMU boot stops.
+
+**Frames** (0x4117b950 + 0x4117a310):
+
+```
+command header, 8 bytes at 0xA04CE37C0 (first 64-byte DMA block):
+  [0] 0x55
+  [1] link sequence counter (0xA04CE3700, ++ each frame)
+  [2] request byte +0x20 (1 or 2; 2 when 0xA04851D8A != 0 -- inferred speed/phase class)
+  [3] command code low byte, [4] high byte (sub-command)
+  [5..6] u16 payload length in 16-bit words = (tx length - 2) / 2
+  [7] checksum: 0x100 - (sum of [0..6]) & 0xff
+data block (0xA04CE5780, 8000-byte buffers):
+  [0] 0x55, payload ..., [last] = -(0x55 + sum of the payload) -- whole block sums to 0
+```
+The task: check pin 41 level (sub_40c15bfc == 0 = lens ready, inferred),
+build the header, set up both directions (sub_40d321bc/sub_40d322cc =
+cache maintenance on the TX/RX buffers), disable the pin-41 irq, start the
+serial transfer (**sub_40ca60e4**(instance, desc 0xA04CE3790), static
+config qword_44ae6400 = {4, 4, 3, 1000}), 5-tick watchdog (timer
+0xA04CE36A8), then wait up to **5010** ticks for completion bit 0 on
+0xA04CE36C8; RX checked by sub_4117bfe8; errors in 0xA04CE376C (1/3 start
+failed, 6 driver error, 9 wrong state). Request +0x2C == 1 selects the
+two-phase path (header, then a separate data phase sized by +0x0E).
+
+Serial setup: sub_40ca5e1c (claim instance), sub_40ca5f24(instance,
+config 0xA02AFF508): config[5] word length (1..8 via byte_42b65320),
+config[6] bit rate in Hz -> divider from an 80 MHz clock
+(div = ceil(80e6 / (2*rate)), actual = 40e6/div), config[7]
+extra bits. **The rate itself is in 0xA02AFF508, which must be read at run
+time** (see the RAM note at the top).
+
+**Command dictionary** (`eg-lenscmd.txt`): RAM table 0xA02B4B350, 48-byte
+records {u16 code, u16 tx length, u16 rx length, u32 +8, u32 +12 (transfer
+type, < 6), u32 +16 (== 1: two-phase), u32 +20, builder fn +24, parser fn
++32, u32 +40, u16 +44 = {wait, retries}}; index -> code: 0..0x5b, e.g. 0 =
+0x10 (28 B), 1 = 0x11 (74 B), 2 = 0x12 (66 B), 3 = 0x13, 6 = 0x1F, 7 = 0x20
+(258 B), 0xe/0xf = 0x24/0x224 (7426 B), 0x10/0x11 = 0x1024/0x1224 (3468 B),
+0x2c..0x33 = 0x0A0..0x7A0, 0x46.. = 0xE0.., 0x57 = 0xF7 (1026 B). Index
+0x1b = code 0x70 is a group: sub-table 0xA02B4C430 (64 records, 0x0370 ..
+0xE970, e.g. 0x3070 receives 7816 B, 0x2F70 194 B). The builder/parser fns
+(0x410987xx-0x4109a9xx / 0x4109a9xx-0x4109d0e4; 0x4109a910 = no payload,
+0x4109d0e4 = status-only reply) are where the field layouts live -- not yet
+read one by one (open). The request is assembled by 0x41096398 (seq,
+args, callback, command index) via 0x41083d70.
+
+## 5. Lens data -> status store
+
+Publisher **0x4106b568** diffs a cache and publishes: 0x2C04 (attached,
+from the lens kind 0xA04831F64 through table 0xA02B44BD8), 0x2C01 focal
+length (field 503 through the u32 table 0xA02B3447C), 0x2C00 focus
+distance (field 500 through 0xA02B31848), 0x2C29 / 0x2C2A min/max focal
+(fields 507 / 508 through 0xA02B3447C), 0x2C1A adapter name (built with a
+format string from bytes of the record at 0xA04831DD0 into 0xA04831CF8),
+0x2C19 lens name (string field 29, or 0xA04831F9C for kind 2) into
+0xA04831D38.
+
+Field getter 0x4109710c(id): descriptor table 0xA02B4D210, 40-byte records
+{mode, buf/offset for lens kind 1, buf/offset for other kinds, getter fn,
+arg}; mode 1 = not for kind 1, mode 2 = only kind 1. **Lens kind 1 = Z
+(ML) lens.** Fields 500/501/503/507/508 live in kind-1 buffer 4 at offsets
+0x0d/0x0e/0x10/0x14/0x15 (getter 0x41097de4); string field 29 (string
+table 0xA02B52EB8) in buffer 7 at +5, 64 bytes. Buffers come from
+sub_41095fbc(buf id): double-buffered images at 0xA04847780 (+0x51E3 or
++0x1FBA per bank, bank bit 0xA04843744 & 1) -- the exact per-buffer offsets
+are in the jump targets at 0x41096010.. (partly read; open), i.e. which
+parser fills buffer 4 / 7 is not pinned yet (inferred: the 0x10/0x11/0x12
+identification replies).
+
+## 6. For the MCU-side names
+
+* MCU kind 1 mode 2 (MCU PB0, "A") = the state the EXPEED sets immediately
+  before the first lens handshake: name it "lens power on (comm)"; mode 0 =
+  off; mode 1 (PA9, "B") is used only by a different sequence
+  (0x41091224) -- inferred a second power level (e.g. motor / high current);
+  no string names it.
+* MCU PF12 (kind 2) = 1 only after identification succeeds, 0 at power-down
+  -> "lens second supply / full-power enable" (inferred).
+* PG4 latch (kind 4/5): armed by 0x4107e8a8 and queried by 0x4107e99c, both
+  next to the lens-detect logic; still unnamed.
+* The 0x91 report is the lens service's only attach trigger (0x41062a58).
+
+## Walls / asks for a run
+
+1. RAM 0xA02AFF508 (lens serial config: word length, bit rate) and
+   0xA02C29000[41], [58], [59], [60] (GPIO handles: port/bit) -- read on a
+   booted machine (hmp xp, A53 space).
+2. Which steps raise the Sysc events 0x04080005..0x0408000c.
+3. The builder/parser bodies per lens command (field layouts) and the
+   buffer-id -> offset map (0x41096010 jump targets).
+4. Dynamic: with a peer that answers pin 58 by pulsing pin 41 (EXPEED port
+   3 bit 10) and clocks serial instance 3, the 0x1F exchange would show
+   the first real frame; nothing in QEMU does that today.
+
+## Resolved after the fact (parent, 2026-10-19, QEMU run `egr`, hmp xp)
+
+* Wall 1. Lens serial config 0xA02AFF508 = u32 {1, 0, 0 (byte +8), 1, 1, 0, 8000000, 0x10}:
+  config[6] = **8 000 000 Hz** -> divider ceil(80e6 / 16e6) = 5 -> exactly 8 MHz; config[5] = 0
+  (outside 1..8, so the word-length table is not applied); byte +28 = 16 feeds the timeout.
+  Pin handles 0xA02C29000[id] -> {+0 id, +4 port, +8 bit}: 41 = port 3 bit 10 (has an irq
+  record at +0x20), 58 = port 4 bit 11, 59 = port 4 bit 12, 60 = port 4 bit 13 -- the inferred
+  pin rule holds.
+* Step 4 / 5 decisions. Field ids at RAM 0xA02B4A998 = {36, 37}; descriptors (40 bytes at
+  0xA02B4D210 + 40*id: {mode, buf kind1, off kind1, buf other, off other, -, getter, arg}):
+  36 = buffer 0 +0, 37 = buffer 0 +1 (the two bytes of the 0x1F reply, parser 0x4109adac),
+  56 = buffer 0 +0 through getter 0x41097de4 arg 0x27, 92 = buffer 1 +0x5e (byte 13 of the
+  0x10 reply, parser 0x4109a914). 0x1F's single payload byte is 1 at step 4 and 2 at step 5
+  (0x41084230). Step 4 done 0x41087ecc: f36 == 0 -> step 11; else (f56 & 0xFE) == 0 and
+  f37 != 0 -> step 5; else error 3 -> step 80. Step 5 done 0x4108805c: f36 == 0 and f37 != 0
+  -> step 6, else error 3 -> 80. Step 6 done 0x41088174: f92 != 0 -> error 0 -> 80, else 7.
